---
/**
 * About. The only page on the site that links out to the operating entity.
 *
 * The origin story is the strongest trust asset here, because it explains
 * where the vendor list actually came from. Two figures in it are data-driven
 * rather than typed in: the number of years (derived from yearEstablished) and
 * the vendor count (company.vettedVendorCount, null until a real figure
 * exists -- the sentence drops the number rather than printing a guess).
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import EntityLink from '../components/EntityLink.astro';
import { company } from '../lib/data';
import { paths } from '../lib/urls';
import type { Crumb } from '../lib/schema';

const crumbs: Crumb[] = [
  { name: 'Home', path: paths.home },
  { name: 'About', path: paths.about },
];

const yearsReferring = 2026 - company.yearEstablished;
const vendorCount = company.vettedVendorCount;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About HomeToMoved | Singapore Mover Matching"
  description="HomeToMoved is run by the people behind Junk to Clear, clearing Singapore flats and offices since 2009. We match you with movers we have seen work."
  path={paths.about}
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <h1>About {company.tradingName}</h1>
  <p>{company.businessModelStatement}</p>

  <h2>Where this came from</h2>
  <p>
    {company.tradingName} is run by the people behind <EntityLink />, {company.parentBrandDescription} since
    {' '}{company.yearEstablished}.
  </p>
  <p>
    That work put us in people's homes at a particular moment. Customers clearing a flat were usually moving
    out, moving in, or handing over to a landlord. They would ask whether we knew someone who could handle
    the cleaning, or the move, or the bit we did not do. So we would recommend someone.
  </p>
  <p>
    Over {yearsReferring} years of doing that, we learned things you only learn by referring real jobs and
    hearing what happened afterwards. Which vendors turn up when they said they would. Which ones quote low
    and find reasons to charge more once they are inside. Which ones you never hear a complaint about. Some
    vendors we stopped referring after a single job.
  </p>
  <p>
    That list &mdash; {vendorCount !== null ? `the ${vendorCount} vendors` : 'the vendors'} we have actually
    seen work &mdash; is what this site is built on. We are not a directory anyone can pay to join, and we do
    not carry out moves ourselves. We match you with people we would use, and you deal with them directly.
  </p>

  <h2>The entity behind the service</h2>
  <p>
    {company.tradingName} is the trading name of <strong>{company.legalName}</strong>, a Singapore-registered
    company established in {company.yearEstablished}.
  </p>
  <p>We operate {company.operatingHours.map((h) => h.label).join(' and ')}.</p>

  <h2>What we do and do not do</h2>
  <p>
    We take your requirements and pass them to moving vendors who have passed our checks. We do not own
    lorries, employ movers or carry out any move. The contract for the move itself is between you and the
    vendor you choose. <a href={paths.vendorStandards}>How we vet movers</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
